{"name":"Flamboyant Teal","hex":"#129c8b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"flamboyant","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Showy, bold or audacious in behaviour, appearance, style, etc.; ostentatious.","Referring to the final stage of French Gothic architecture from the 14th to the 16th centuries."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The royal poinciana (Delonix regia), a showy tropical tree from Madagascar."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flamboyant"},{"term":"teal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various small freshwater ducks of the genus Anas that are brightly coloured and have short necks.","A dark, somewhat bluish-green colour; a dark cyan."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a bluish-green colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/teal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Flamboyant","blocks":[{"text":"Flamboyant is a lavishly decorated style of Gothic architecture that appeared in France and Spain in the 15th century, and lasted until the mid-sixteenth century and the beginning of the Renaissance. Elaborate stone tracery covered both the exterior and the interior. Windows were decorated with a characteristic s-shaped curve. Masonry wall space was reduced further as windows grew even larger. Major examples included the northern spire of Chartres Cathedral, Trinity Abbey, Vendôme, and Burgos Cathedral and Segovia Cathedral in Spain. It was gradually replaced by Renaissance architecture in the 16th century."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Vend%C3%B4me_Abbatiale_de_la_Trinit%C3%A9_Fassade_5.jpg/330px-Vend%C3%B4me_Abbatiale_de_la_Trinit%C3%A9_Fassade_5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flamboyant"},{"title":"Teal","blocks":[{"text":"Teal is a dark cyan color. Its name comes from that of a bird, the Eurasian teal which has a similarly colored stripe on its head. The word is often used colloquially to refer to shades of cyan in general."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Smithsonian_-_NMAAHC_-_Teal_blue_dress_and_cropped_jacket_designed_by_Ann_Lowe-_NMAAHC_2014.73.2.1-.2.jpg/330px-Smithsonian_-_NMAAHC_-_Teal_blue_dress_and_cropped_jacket_designed_by_Ann_Lowe-_NMAAHC_2014.73.2.1-.2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teal"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/L%E2%80%99%C3%89pine_%28Marne%29_Notre-Dame_020.jpg/500px-L%E2%80%99%C3%89pine_%28Marne%29_Notre-Dame_020.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/L%E2%80%99%C3%89pine_%28Marne%29_Notre-Dame_020.jpg/1280px-L%E2%80%99%C3%89pine_%28Marne%29_Notre-Dame_020.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/L%E2%80%99%C3%89pine_%28Marne%29_Notre-Dame_020.jpg/500px-L%E2%80%99%C3%89pine_%28Marne%29_Notre-Dame_020.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Notre-Dame de l'Épine, west front (1405–1527)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AL%E2%80%99%C3%89pine_(Marne)_Notre-Dame_020.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/El_reino_de_los_cielos.JPG/500px-El_reino_de_los_cielos.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/El_reino_de_los_cielos.JPG/1280px-El_reino_de_los_cielos.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/El_reino_de_los_cielos.JPG/500px-El_reino_de_los_cielos.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Flamboyant rib vaulting of Segov